1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,664
Your chatbot answers.

2
00:00:01,814 --> 00:00:03,222
Why can't it act?

3
00:00:03,722 --> 00:00:05,152
If you are building AI

4
00:00:05,152 --> 00:00:07,623
projects, this difference decides what

5
00:00:07,623 --> 00:00:09,183
you actually build next.

6
00:00:09,683 --> 00:00:11,207
A chatbot is a software

7
00:00:11,207 --> 00:00:13,922
application that communicates with people

8
00:00:13,922 --> 00:00:15,379
through text or voice.

9
00:00:15,529 --> 00:00:16,867
Ask it when your exam

10
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:18,396
is, and it answers, then

11
00:00:18,396 --> 00:00:20,180
waits for your next message.

12
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:21,982
An agent is different: a

13
00:00:21,982 --> 00:00:24,666
system that autonomously performs tasks

14
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:27,213
by designing workflows with available

15
00:00:27,213 --> 00:00:27,626
tools.

16
00:00:27,776 --> 00:00:28,963
Give it a goal like

17
00:00:28,963 --> 00:00:31,211
"shortlist internships that match my

18
00:00:31,211 --> 00:00:32,959
résumé and add the deadlines

19
00:00:32,959 --> 00:00:34,396
to my calendar", and it

20
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:36,457
plans the steps, searches, reads,

21
00:00:36,457 --> 00:00:38,518
shortlists and writes the entries

22
00:00:38,518 --> 00:00:38,955
itself.

23
00:00:39,105 --> 00:00:41,606
Anthropic describes agents as systems

24
00:00:41,606 --> 00:00:43,431
where the model directs its

25
00:00:43,431 --> 00:00:45,121
own process and tool use.

26
00:00:45,621 --> 00:00:47,306
So here is the test.

27
00:00:47,456 --> 00:00:48,995
If it only talks, it

28
00:00:48,995 --> 00:00:49,995
is a chatbot.

29
00:00:50,145 --> 00:00:51,492
If it pursues a goal

30
00:00:51,492 --> 00:00:53,379
and completes tasks for you,

31
00:00:53,379 --> 00:00:54,390
it is an agent.

32
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:58,261
Explore AI learning at ziro.digital.
